      "knowledge_point": "Expressing a Compound Predicate in Symbolic Form",
      "problem": "Consider the following compound predicates:\n\n$x$ is even **and** divisible by $5.$ \n\n$x$ is even **or** less than $6$.\n\nExpress these compound predicates above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $B(x):$ $x$ is divisible by $5$\n\n- $C(x):$ $x$ is less than $6$",
      "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\land.$\" \n\nSo, the first sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099242/assets/6e906074c9243c4189238c6ef5606954422bb7b8d2d3ad0b373579d25e221bb7.png)\n\nthat is, $A \\land B.$\n\nMoreover, the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\\lor.$\" \n\nSo, the second sentence reads\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14099242/assets/e557113d18858d98a329fe4ce3ba84754defdc652095ccf57844077b7426d154.png)\n\nthat is, $A \\lor C.$",
      "difficulty": null,
      "answer_fields": [],
